## June is supposed to be a down month in plumbing. We turned it into a 33% year-over-year gain.

Drain Mob is a family-owned San Diego drain and plumbing company. Plumbing has a seasonal shape, and June is soft: the prior year, revenue fell high single digits from May to June. This year that reversed - revenue **rose** high single digits from May to June, in the month the business normally contracts.

## What we built.

- **Search and AI foundation.** LocalBusiness, Service, and FAQPage schema; title and meta rewrites; an author and E-E-A-T build; and Core Web Vitals cleanup.
- **Paid, restructured.** We moved Google Ads out of Performance Max into a manual Search build with intent-specific ad groups, and fixed demographic overspend on Meta.
- **Lifecycle automation.** An eight-automation lifecycle system in ServiceTitan Marketing Pro covering post-job review capture, reactivation, and referral.

## What happened.

- **Year-over-year revenue up 33% in June and 11% in May.**
- **June reversed its usual decline** - down high single digits May to June the prior year, up high single digits May to June this year.
- **Surfacing consistently across ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Claude** following the schema rebuild.

> The growth is real, but the tell is the timing: we posted the biggest year-over-year gain in the exact month the trade expects to lose ground.
